    "unresolved": [
      "No owner is evidenced. The notes list roles only; the Director of Environment and Place chaired, and chairing is not ownership. No individual is named.",
      "The highways context is recorded in the notes of the decision's own day; read as whole-day intervals its contemporaneity is indeterminate and it cannot be presented as contemporaneous context.",
      "The board refers to 'the expected annual saving' without citing a figure or the business case. SRC-03 §4 is attached on subject matter only; it pre-dates the meeting, and nothing settles whether it was before the board (considered: unknown).",
      "The notes do not say under what authority the board agreed. Whether retaining Northgate was within officer delegation (SRC-01 §3.1, §3.3) or a commitment reserved to Cabinet (§3.2: altering the service footprint in more than one ward) is not evidenced; SRC-01 is not cited.",
      "Cabinet considered consolidating three depots onto Calder Road (brackwell-2) and required a further site-selection report before contracts are let (brackwell-4). The notes refer to neither, so no lineage is contributed and neither supersession nor conflict is asserted.",
      "SRC-06 (30 June 2026) records two rounds running out of Northgate rather than Calder Road. Whether that is consistent with Northgate 'retained for vehicle storage' is not settled (see brackwell-6)."
    ],
